6,"Kovai Language (KQB) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level & Official Use | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kqb/,Kovai is a stable indigenous language of Papua New Guinea. It belongs to the Trans-New Guinea language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Kovai,Trans-New Guinea
7,Kovai | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kqb/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..2eiBdtH8a3NlhC0ZHJOk0aCAkKWDjEMapQTcR-u7ly4,Kovai is a stable indigenous language of Papua New Guinea. It belongs to the Trans-New Guinea language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Kovai,Trans-New Guinea
8,PeopleGroups.org - Kovai of Papua New Guinea,https://www.peoplegroups.org/explore/GroupDetails.aspx?peid=10094,"Overview: The Kovai of Papua New Guinea, numbering 9,700, are No Longer Unreached. They are part of the New Guinea people cluster within the Pacific Islanders affinity bloc. This people group is only found in Papua New Guinea. Their primary language is Kovai.",Kovai,Trans-New Guinea
9,music of guinea,http://www.muzikifan.com/guinee.html,"There's a general rule of logic that you should not buy your music twice. Apart from buying an album and finding you have it already, maybe with a different cover, which is a mistake anyone can make. A big reset in music listening habits occurred when the CD was introduced in the early 1980s ...",Kovai,Trans-New Guinea
